    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "2TI",
      "chapter": 1,
      "chapter_usfm": "2TI.1",
      "version_id": 4669,
      "version_abbr": "AFINT",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, in accordance with the promise of life which is in Christ Jesus,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "To Timothy, beloved child: Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord."
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I am grateful to God, whom I serve with a clear conscience as my forefathers did,* as I constantly remember you in my prayers night and day,*"
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "longing to see you as I remember your tears, that I may be filled with joy."
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I am reminded of the sincere faith in you,* which lived first in your grandmother Lois and your mother Eunice, and I am convinced that it is in you also."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For this* reason, I remind you to stir into flame the gift of God that is in you through the laying on of my hands."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For God did not give us a spirit of cowardice, but of power and love and self-control."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Therefore, do not be ashamed of the testimony about our Lord, nor of me, His prisoner, but take part in suffering for the gospel by the power of God,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "who saved us and called us with a holy calling, not according to our works, but according to His own purpose and grace, which was given to us in Christ Jesus before the beginning of the ages,*"
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "but has now been manifested by the appearing of our Saviour, Jesus Christ,* who vanquished death and brought life and immortality to light through the gospel,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "for which I was appointed a preacher and an apostle and a teacher."
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For this* reason, I also suffer these things; but I am not ashamed, for I know whom I have believed, and I am convinced that He is able to guard the deposit entrusted to me until that day."
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Hold the pattern of sound words* which you heard from me, in faith and love that are in Christ Jesus."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Guard the good deposit entrusted to you by the Holy Spirit who lives in us."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "You are aware of this, that all those in Asia turned away from me, among whom are Phygelus and Hermogenes."
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "May the Lord grant mercy to the household of Onesiphorus, because he frequently refreshed me and was not ashamed of my imprisonment;*"
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "but when he was in Rome, he eagerly sought me and found me."
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "2TI.1.18",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "May the Lord grant him to find mercy from the Lord on that day!—and you are very well aware of how greatly he served me in Ephesus. 3 Greek whom I serve from my forefathers with a clear conscience 3 Greek as I have constant remembrance about you in my prayers night and day 5 Greek having received remembrance of the sincere faith in you 6 Greek which 9 Greek eternal times 10 Some ancient manuscripts read Jesus Christ 12 Greek which 13 Greek words that are being sound 16 Greek chain"
        }
      ],
