    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "2TI",
      "chapter": 2,
      "chapter_usfm": "2TI.2",
      "version_id": 4669,
      "version_abbr": "AFINT",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "You, therefore, my child, be strong in the grace that is in Christ Jesus,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and the things which you have heard from me in the presence of many witnesses, entrust these to faithful men* who will be competent to teach others also."
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Take part in my suffering as a good soldier of Christ Jesus."
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "No one who serves as a soldier becomes entangled in the affairs of daily life, so that he may please the one who enlisted him."
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "And if anyone likewise competes as an athlete, he is not crowned unless he competes according to the rules."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "The farmer who works hard must be the first to receive a share of the produce.*"
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Consider what I am saying, for the Lord will grant you insight into all these things."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Remember Jesus Christ, raised from the dead, the offspring of David, according to my gospel,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "for which I suffer affliction to the point of imprisonment* as a criminal, but the word of God is not bound."
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For this reason, I endure all things for the sake of the elect, so that they also may obtain the salvation that is in Christ Jesus with eternal glory."
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "The saying is trustworthy: For if we died with Him,we will also live with Him;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "if we endure, we will also reign with Him;if we deny Him,He also will deny us;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "if we are unfaithful, He remains faithful,for He cannot deny Himself."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Remind people of these things, earnestly charging them before God* not to quarrel about words—a practice that is useful for nothing* and only leads to the ruin of the hearers."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Endeavour earnestly to present yourself approved to God, a worker who has no need to be ashamed, correctly handling the word of truth."
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But avoid worldly and empty discussions, for they will lead to more and more ungodliness,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and their teaching will spread like gangrene. Among them* are Hymenaeus and Philetus."
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.18",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "who have deviated in regard to the truth by asserting that the resurrection has already taken place, and they are subverting the faith of some."
        },
        {
          "verse": 19,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.19",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "However, the firm foundation of God stands, having this seal: “The Lord knows those who are His,” and “Let everyone who names the name of the Lord depart from unrighteousness.”*"
        },
        {
          "verse": 20,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.20",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Now in a great house, there are not only vessels of gold and silver but also of wood and clay, some for* honour and some for* dishonour."
        },
        {
          "verse": 21,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.21",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Therefore, if anyone cleanses himself from these things, he will be a vessel for honour, sanctified, useful to the Master, prepared for every good work."
        },
        {
          "verse": 22,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.22",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Now flee from youthful desires, and pursue righteousness, faith, love, and peace, along with those who call on the Lord from a pure heart."
        },
        {
          "verse": 23,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.23",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But shun foolish and ignorant controversies, knowing that they generate quarrels."
        },
        {
          "verse": 24,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.24",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "And the servant of the Lord must not quarrel, but be gentle towards everyone, competent in teaching, enduring evil with patience,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 25,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.25",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "instructing opponents* with gentleness, if perhaps God may grant them repentance, resulting in a knowledge of the truth,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 26,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.26",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and they may regain their senses and escape from the trap of the devil, having been captured by him for the purpose of doing* his will. 2 Or people, as the term is used in a generic sense 6 Greek fruits 9 Greek to the point of chains 14 Some ancient manuscripts replace God with Lord 14 Greek useful for nothing 17 Greek whom 19 Alluded to Is. 26:13 20 Greek some of which 25 Greek those who oppose 26 The participle doing is supplied to the text on contextual considerations for the sake of clarity"
        }
      ],
